t(22, 1240, """A mother who throws her eight children to their paternal grandmother after their father's death and seizes the deceased father's pension! The basic principle in woman is fixed: she was not created and not formed by nature to bear responsibility, and her nature always makes her need a man's support, and she collapses psychologically with the mere departure of the man; and whoever keeps resisting gets afflicted with psychological and organic diseases, then collapses sooner or later, a collapse certain to happen even if delayed. The model story is an expression of the absence of a conscience mixed with a nature that, if the devils of mankind and jinn among the advocates of feminism gathered to change it, they would not change a mustard seed's weight of it. The results of burdening woman with responsibility: either she is patient and lives wronged and sick with diseases, or she loses her mind and commits suicide, or she loses her conscience; as for the righteous one, she lives grief, weeping and diseases and bears the upbringing of the children, and the like of her are like a lone star in a pitch-black sky.""")

t(23, 160, """We do not sleep! We are too weak to sleep! If Allah wills that we not sleep, we do not sleep! Sleep is among the greatest blessings whose worth many people do not feel! Sleep is a pure Lordly gift, not a human effort as many people imagine! If our Mighty Lord, holy are His names, exalted in the heavens and the earth, exalted greatly, willed to withdraw sleep, then woe to the one from whom it is withdrawn! He lives complete woe and wishes for death and does not find it! Sleep is a gift from Allah the Exalted that many people think is a given! Many people think sleep is a self-evident and spontaneous matter, and that he will certainly and inevitably sleep whenever he wishes! The truth is that the matter is the exact opposite!""")

h(23, 800, """(Al-Naba: 9); that is, rest for your bodies and a cutting off of movement so the limbs may rest. • The verse of reflection: {And among His signs is your sleep by night and day...} (Al-Rum: 23); Allah considered sleep by night and day among the proofs of His great power. • The verse of stillness: {It is He who made the night for you to rest in...} (Yunus: 67) and (Ghafir: 61). • The verse of clothing: {And it is He who made the night for you...""")

